<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Dar Tama</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1912 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small sultanate of the Tama people in the hills of eastern Chad, long fought over by its powerful neighbours Wadai and Darfur.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tama-people">Tama</a>, who speak a language of the Taman group, formed a sultanate in the hills around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guereda">Guéréda</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a> by the 17th century. It lay on the frontier between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultans ruled a farming and herding population from hilltop villages, relying on rough terrain for defence. Dar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tama-people">Tama</a> paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a> for most of its history, while sometimes turning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> for support. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> was adopted by the ruling house, and little else is known in detail.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>French forces occupied eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a> after defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a> in 1909, and Dar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tama-people">Tama</a> came under French control around 1912. Its sultan became a traditional chief within the colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chad-french-colony">Chad (French colony)</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1600 CE – 1912 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:6.21%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1912 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tama</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Chad</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tama sultanate, Sultanate of Tama</dd></dl></aside></div>

